      }
    }
  ],
  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.580791666666666,
      "text": "A recipe, a ribbon and a walking track all hide fraction puzzles.",
      "source_sha256": "bac512b543ea9c174127bc9f17074e5c1fd30664a02f7a70098dc4cac0ee617d"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.7007916666666665,
      "end": 7.652166666666667,
      "text": "Your first job isn't to grab the numbers.",
      "source_sha256": "7d78fb1c46a0cd61eef6069d48e7a3291e3268d5fc64c75795f223c9da7c0a28"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.772166666666666,
      "end": 11.099541666666667,
      "text": "It's to discover what the story is really asking!",
      "source_sha256": "960abbcdbd99239365f1b7095f91856a81e4144d3887cd4b69a16b26e2ce3451"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.8,
      "end": 19.572,
      "text": "Today, we're learning to interpret everyday fraction problems, choose a suitable strategy, and explain a solution that makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "575b9aeb554a6c2a1c7aa36a8d0237e9c40fd83b21c48beccc812729e139bcdf"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.2,
      "end": 25.060416666666665,
      "text": "You'll identify the whole and the unit, so you know what each fraction describes.",
      "source_sha256": "d8c314bfaea2f5c2957750b0f58a30e565b91115d2bcecdfb9c49a871757627a"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.266666666666666,
      "end": 29.268291666666666,
      "text": "You'll choose an operation and make a model before you calculate.",
      "source_sha256": "a5e787f9e2de1fa86440c79dad05f86392cf2d0d949868e960c93282750df5c7"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.5,
      "end": 33.71666666666667,
      "text": "You'll explain your answer with its unit, then check it against the story.",
      "source_sha256": "f65eaa6960932e74a8a4aa60edfb19c858207c2ccd614a1c98e9561eb475229e"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.93333333333333,
      "end": 35.50366666666667,
      "text": "First, choose one whole.",
      "source_sha256": "02a83516a6b2b91cb63233805332a75b24fd3de360190176bd7ac3be70517d21"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.623666666666665,
      "end": 38.34,
      "text": "Its parts must be equal in size.",
      "source_sha256": "0cbe161dd0fb517b64fcca4bb3be2e30ba8bea5988a0538e37a5588276468a71"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.46,
      "end": 43.097,
      "text": "The outline of the model shows the entire whole, not just the coloured share.",
      "source_sha256": "9ccf68f017bede69c3d5aefbdfa22bed09831f89ce330c59a97e159fb4d99e0d"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.6,
      "end": 46.81366666666667,
      "text": "Here, three equal parts are chosen out of four.",
      "source_sha256": "20ab84718b87a6d8eb864d2166f554daa948b8ee74fe201783fe997c0e6fc8f8"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.93366666666667,
      "end": 50.52758333333333,
      "text": "The top number, the numerator, counts chosen parts.",
      "source_sha256": "2f60b8c1291421532326831678f8112a84afb0f2a5994f9102d8f9f32da97319"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.64758333333333,
      "end": 55.263,
      "text": "The bottom number, the denominator, tells how many equal parts make the whole.",
      "source_sha256": "92b15bc6a5e14907b86f7b0106f92a72ea5a1ffb72d943feb1cb6e63c8972e28"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.86666666666667,
      "end": 60.46391666666667,
      "text": "A recipe uses half a cup of oats and a quarter of a cup of nuts.",
      "source_sha256": "6c9a2b1db7724d16aa14212b3cca4a132b95ad88b148788aa151bcda07adf0a4"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.58391666666667,
      "end": 64.2145,
      "text": "What operation fits the question: how much altogether?",
      "source_sha256": "022e36f8be1e7c99249d9f39b121ba449d95b38b4b632424649d3e6601d80be6"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.23333333333333,
      "end": 70.066875,
      "text": "First identify the whole: one cup.",
      "source_sha256": "012a0299bdbf31d37315084943c6489e16a636750ad2e479280cf7a0aacd7c79"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.186875,
      "end": 74.26675,
      "text": "Altogether tells us to combine the amounts, so choose addition.",
      "source_sha256": "e9663a1436c72d6cb52741880d39d7bc3d975cf8511daf9ac31a16ccab6b516d"
    },
    {
      "start": 74.63333333333334,
      "end": 77.20254166666666,
      "text": "Rename one half as two quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "40d3519b5f57bbe90b69fed0c708531e5cd9822e6780cdbfef8a8c4b79b9f939"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.32254166666667,
      "end": 80.64725,
      "text": "Two quarters plus one quarter makes three quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "bab85ca83de93e6f0665dce3c1b3f6e1496d681a215531c57ed432d043f3a1df"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.0,
      "end": 84.53416666666666,
      "text": "Mia uses three quarters of a cup altogether.",
      "source_sha256": "d42456cefdec6a667a66c1e5032d2d5658ee9ad6f26950a7f3906d7d5c22f938"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.65416666666667,
      "end": 89.376875,
      "text": "That is more than half a cup and less than one cup, so the answer makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "bf2110180088d204693763a39450d928a49b11452c8fd3cdf9774c8f0ec8a505"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.73333333333333,
      "end": 94.44066666666667,
      "text": "A useful answer tells the amount and its unit: three quarters of a cup.",
      "source_sha256": "4afa42199826f7ec3e10457e824f6b51e74e71309fa30f4bc1158c992302977e"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.56066666666666,
      "end": 100.33308333333333,
      "text": "Compare it with the ingredients to check that nothing has disappeared or been counted twice.",
      "source_sha256": "3c80095d2e3621d4f24b18c7eef54ba443fb9cb57f36e0cef595951667d52b06"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.0,
      "end": 103.19008333333333,
      "text": "A ribbon is two metres long.",
      "source_sha256": "683520282be29da4d4726d744aa48f44c8dfbf74fed0ff8bacb36930e466153c"
    },
    {
      "start": 103.31008333333334,
      "end": 105.70095833333333,
      "text": "We cut off three quarters of a metre.",
      "source_sha256": "5c14879fa16056261394eb194d32c741104a39774a1e4b904253eb47af548a5b"
    },
    {
      "start": 105.82095833333334,
      "end": 108.969375,
      "text": "Will the remaining length be more or less than one metre?",
      "source_sha256": "0a48c0081adfbaaa34550cde506b36654a0fcbb66c4043d3f339dc06025b1a15"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.0,
      "end": 114.606375,
      "text": "Now a ribbon is two metres long.",
      "source_sha256": "a36975f033ed5bd82086bdc42f8e56df4fe954225e3a1e48ea333646d824f355"
    },
    {
      "start": 114.726375,
      "end": 117.17495833333334,
      "text": "We cut off three quarters of a metre.",
      "source_sha256": "e80a34415593b29b731430aa6e639b85bacc6c38bbbf9a86d4314bdb7493e12d"
    },
    {
      "start": 117.29495833333333,
      "end": 119.26179166666667,
      "text": "How much ribbon remains?",
      "source_sha256": "4ff29e616fa1ee10a9da9b57bcd32692de48417835274189055ddeecc25290be"
    },
    {
      "start": 119.63333333333334,
      "end": 122.24841666666667,
      "text": "We want what remains, so subtract.",
      "source_sha256": "d8c289000eb61828079709ac24f017b15a061c7c210e1cf52f0a8c034d2dff69"
    },
    {
      "start": 122.36841666666666,
      "end": 125.13420833333333,
      "text": "Two metres equals eight quarter-metres.",
      "source_sha256": "c42734a409a06005be6279b3e258ff77f969a7585ebbe826d925269acac7604d"
    },
    {
      "start": 125.5,
      "end": 129.297875,
      "text": "Eight quarters minus three quarters is five quarters.",
      "source_sha256": "7c1a21117f5592b3328c38464ec63754991784e55486b27afaa367434b34b45b"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.417875,
      "end": 132.2085,
      "text": "Five quarters is one and one quarter.",
      "source_sha256": "8687ad6c8ebd8d57a2e9df1be51cd0c15523dcf20b0e53c031a5afaa98e4c988"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.56666666666666,
      "end": 135.15179166666667,
      "text": "One and one quarter metres remain.",
      "source_sha256": "3efdadc709998c67b4f6a01df445bc27c96d284de5f96b166248445b960f18b9"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.27179166666667,
      "end": 138.847375,
      "text": "On the number line, move back three quarter-steps from two.",
      "source_sha256": "1bfe95e53adc0538a9a4279c327eeb345f7134ade0481d074ad51c88708dafe1"
    },
    {
      "start": 139.2,
      "end": 144.22708333333333,
      "text": "The three quarters refers to one metre, not three quarters of the two-metre ribbon.",
      "source_sha256": "12c04586bca3f7a6fc7e188963449fe645c3192ca9d45ed94a46344b55576fca"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.34708333333333,
      "end": 148.59183333333334,
      "text": "Naming the unit clearly prevents a very different calculation.",
      "source_sha256": "05f6974cb66e92f89510b76c5be39053831d1e8899b0f45620ad44cf5e48cb44"
    },
    {
      "start": 149.26666666666668,
      "end": 153.11383333333333,
      "text": "For a comparison, Ava walks three quarters of a kilometre.",
      "source_sha256": "ecb0f5b1857fbbfdf1f1eb86db4797836406dac852ddd30bdc4cb5e7c2e1286c"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.23383333333334,
      "end": 156.02845833333333,
      "text": "Leo walks five eighths of a kilometre.",
      "source_sha256": "4a79d21fe372699ada4262669bdf43ee6979169e2590e9603200ea01851dee6f"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.14845833333334,
      "end": 158.71354166666666,
      "text": "Who walks farther, and by how much?",
      "source_sha256": "0db278f4a1e1e227a56024c90717a62374e8383cadef2851ef3aaf76404496c5"
    },
    {
      "start": 159.06666666666666,
      "end": 161.73333333333332,
      "text": "Rename three quarters as six eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "5819ec3c1ff71ad6955df1910990faab1d113ee9d9470d2174bb966879c74844"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.85333333333332,
      "end": 166.19054166666666,
      "text": "Ava walks farther because six eighths is greater than five eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "bde5c7dc19a9e0382482fc3a8465eda6df1c71e51abec994f9b91118a6aa1f79"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.56666666666666,
      "end": 169.31704166666665,
      "text": "Subtract five eighths from six eighths.",
      "source_sha256": "a478bd1c5cb348e4243ed2f4e1725722649bdc14d7fc3dabd630f4f4e1c3bec2"
    },
    {
      "start": 169.43704166666666,
      "end": 172.570375,
      "text": "Ava walks one eighth of a kilometre farther.",
      "source_sha256": "5f9321af79830351cda2d62f9ae2bbc8476697dfe72c58cff75454ce81a461ab"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.93333333333334,
      "end": 175.04408333333333,
      "text": "Here is a two-step problem.",
      "source_sha256": "c613863edf999bb93245db8ab55922ed11d213cfd3988337d79587f348f62db2"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.16408333333334,
      "end": 177.13566666666668,
      "text": "A jug holds one litre.",
      "source_sha256": "ea21dd5f3cf4013a3c50429a83518d16f1ed87d09f25d5c8301bf2b2d0b575d0"
    },
    {
      "start": 177.25566666666666,
      "end": 180.64158333333333,
      "text": "We pour out a quarter of a litre, then another half a litre.",
      "source_sha256": "d6e1b3c1fd21a2b67ef86b98f11a5fff8f2eca2ebe465e3c2d034161df73e343"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.76158333333333,
      "end": 182.34675,
      "text": "How much remains?",
      "source_sha256": "f4976c94e19495a828a03b797f38876f43e0f0606e039aa2f17bb788a15b3b90"
    },
    {
      "start": 182.7,
      "end": 186.64758333333333,
      "text": "A quarter plus a half is three quarters of a litre poured out.",
      "source_sha256": "588091108d3d6bd5241c66301bab51579a90c29e6e3eadf8fe7cef3cd089ff60"
    },
    {
      "start": 186.76758333333333,
      "end": 189.72629166666667,
      "text": "Subtract three quarters from one whole litre.",
      "source_sha256": "1bd0f9db25c7c39701328c80e0953812def2fa23adecbeaef346d14e9876bb38"
    },
    {
      "start": 190.1,
      "end": 192.49520833333332,
      "text": "One quarter of a litre remains.",
      "source_sha256": "164f85adf023c20d4743d65da55f276fb940a07a2a4d56e8a39a8cb89670a7c0"
    },
    {
      "start": 192.61520833333333,
      "end": 197.37054166666667,
      "text": "Check: three quarters poured out plus one quarter remaining makes one whole litre.",
      "source_sha256": "27a354035e7f0f23e83eafb469e2f1f5f04a35e07d335112bbb0a29b3a39514b"
    },
    {
      "start": 197.73333333333332,
      "end": 201.163125,
      "text": "You walk two thirds of a kilometre, then one sixth more.",
      "source_sha256": "71a6974d774a089df071a146e3db7229463c7cfdff1a84377e736e8495dac32a"
    },
    {
      "start": 201.283125,
      "end": 203.67425,
      "text": "How far is that altogether?",
      "source_sha256": "af01aeb74e5de9eac75656340b47280d9749f7fa56a9dcda436c40e84c252fa6"
    },
    {
      "start": 208.7,
      "end": 210.81454166666666,
      "text": "Two thirds is four sixths.",
      "source_sha256": "6a0117e6d0cc0e65af24b11f203de5a9183304a9cd6709b231accc9186a27bb3"
    },
    {
      "start": 210.93454166666666,
      "end": 214.16429166666666,
      "text": "Adding one sixth gives five sixths of a kilometre.",
      "source_sha256": "980db3b88191fafbc28f8361d1088f0603af257d9c7f501b22bf2b28f886b956"
    },
    {
      "start": 214.53333333333333,
      "end": 218.73258333333334,
      "text": "Our goal was to solve and explain everyday fraction problems.",
      "source_sha256": "58c59153d882c7e5888dd866ccda8b40a48a6522023d5209929862573447a885"
    },
    {
      "start": 218.85258333333334,
      "end": 223.63579166666668,
      "text": "Identify the whole, model the relationship, calculate and check the unit.",
      "source_sha256": "dbfe5adccb1c6ef9e97e913cf0103092baf3fd5c75a32e8613fda96058d7ec63"
    },
    {
      "start": 223.75579166666665,
      "end": 227.35491666666667,
      "text": "Could you invent a fraction story about your own day?",
      "source_sha256": "c0904b019429e2ed332a8550017e4544c4b6885f78e1dfb0fa024761c7ff7836"
    },
    {
      "start": 227.47491666666667,
      "end": 231.157375,
      "text": "Give it a try, then explore the practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "d51e46f7ff542ee50ab26b622fd0665e63c27ee0ab699598c5d4afc4d70e3c91"
    }
  ],
